# Proof: F-V3-FIFO
# Top: v3_fifo, parameterized to the TX configuration (WIDTH 8, PUSH_MAX 4),
#   the widest push and so the hardest atomicity case.
# Assumptions: initial sampled reset; arbitrary subsequent inputs.
# Properties: reset clears the pointers and level; occupancy never exceeds
#   DEPTH; the level tracks accepted pushes and pops; the write pointer moves
#   only for an accepted push and a rejected push writes nothing; the read
#   pointer advances only on an accepted pop; an accepted push lands its first
#   entry at the old write pointer; the head is the oldest entry.
# Method: temporal induction; bounded success alone is insufficient.
# Scope and abstractions: formal/README.md.

read_verilog -formal src/v3_fifo.v
chparam -set WIDTH 8 -set PUSH_MAX 4 v3_fifo
prep -top v3_fifo
flatten
memory_map
opt
async2sync
dffunmap
sat -seq 4 -tempinduct -maxsteps 16 -set-assumes -prove-asserts -verify
